LICENCE TO USE THE COPERNICUS MARINE SERVICE PRODUCTS

IMPORTANT NOTICE: PLEASE READ CAREFULLY BEFORE USING COPERNICUS MARINE SERVICE PRODUCTS. This Licence Agreement is a legal agreement between the Licensee and MERCATOR OCEAN and sets out the terms for use of the Copernicus Marine Service Products and information which will apply to the Licensee. Use of the Copernicus Marine Service Products means that the Licensee agrees to abide by all of the terms and conditions in this Licence.
Introduction

(i) The Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service is funded since 2014 under the Regulation (EU) N°377/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 3 April 2014 establishing the Copernicus Programme and then, under the EU Regulation (EU) 2021/696 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 28 April 2021 establishing the Union Space Programme and the European Union Agency for the Space Programme.

(ii) The legal entity entrusted by the Delegation Agreement signed on 11th November 2014 to implement the Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service is MERCATOR OCEAN, renewed by the European Commission within the Contribution Agreement signed on 22nd July 2021 as the entrusted entity to implement the Copernicus component of the space programme of the European Union for the Copernicus Marine Service.

(iii) The Copernicus Marine Service Products are products listed in the Copernicus Marine Service catalogue, maintained by MERCATOR OCEAN.
1.Interpretation and Definitions
Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service	means the Copernicus Marine Service operation under the terms of the Regulation (EU) N° 377/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 3 April 2014 establishing the Copernicus Programme and the EU Regulation (EU) 2021/696 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 28 April 2021 establishing the Union Space Programme and the European Union Agency for the Space Programme;
Copernicus Marine Service Product(s)	means those products created by the Copernicus Marine Service made available for use under the Copernicus Marine Service catalogue;
Copernicus Marine Service Catalogue	means the list of Copernicus Marine Service Products made available via the Copernicus Marine Service website to the Licensee at any given time;

Derivative Work
	means any product and/or information which has been derived, developed and irreversibly modified from Copernicus Marine Service Product(s) or Value Added Product(s) and does not retain the original pixel structure of a Copernicus Marine Service Product;
Digital Object Identifiers	means persistent and stable references for scientific data, and enable data for each Copernicus Marine Product to be easily and reliably found, used and cited.
Copernicus Marine Service Information	means any drawings, reports, papers, or any other technical information, know-how, products, data or documents of any king, including oral information available from the Copernicus Marine Service website or issued from any Copernicus Marine Service events.

