6. Breach of this Licence

6.1 When MERCATOR OCEAN considers that a breach of this Licence has occurred, it may at its discretion take such action as deemed appropriate.
Failure to comply with the terms and conditions of the Licence Permissions constitutes a material breach of the terms of use for which the Licensee is permitted to use the Copernicus Marine Service Products and may result in the Copernicus Marine Service taking all or any of the following actions.

(a) Immediate, temporary or permanent withdrawal of the Licensee’s right to use the Copernicus Marine Service Products.

(b) Issue a warning to the Licensee.

(c) Legal proceedings against the Licensee for reimbursement of all costs on an indemnity basis (including but not limited to reasonable administrative and legal costs) resulting from the breach.

(d) Disclosure of such information to law enforcement authorities as the MERCATOR OCEAN feels is necessary or as required by law.

6.2 MERCATOR OCEAN excludes its liability for all action it may take in response to breaches of this Licence. The actions described above are not limited, and MERCATOR OCEAN may take any other action it deems appropriate.

6.3 The Licensee will indemnify MERCATOR OCEAN against breach of this Licence.
